      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;bowers--wilkins-px7-s3-vs-bose-quietcomfort-ultra-2&#34;&gt;Bowers &amp;amp; Wilkins Px7 S3 vs. Bose QuietComfort Ultra 2&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img&#xA;        class=&#34;lazyload&#34;&#xA;        src=&#34;https://www.theexpattech.com/svg/loading.min.svg&#34;&#xA;        data-src=&#34;https://www.theexpattech.com/tech-tips/px7-s3-vs-bose-qc-ultra-2/px7-vs-bose.jpg&#34;&#xA;        data-srcset=&#34;https://www.theexpattech.com/tech-tips/px7-s3-vs-bose-qc-ultra-2/px7-vs-bose.jpg, https://www.theexpattech.com/tech-tips/px7-s3-vs-bose-qc-ultra-2/px7-vs-bose.jpg 1.5x, https://www.theexpattech.com/tech-tips/px7-s3-vs-bose-qc-ultra-2/px7-vs-bose.jpg 2x&#34;&#xA;        data-sizes=&#34;auto&#34;&#xA;        alt=&#34;/tech-tips/px7-s3-vs-bose-qc-ultra-2/px7-vs-bose.jpg&#34;&#xA;        title=&#34;Bowers &amp;amp; Wilkins Px7 S3 vs Bose QuietComfort Ultra 2&#34; width=&#34;600&#34; height=&#34;800&#34; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;a-real-world-comparison-for-people-who-actually-care-about-sound&#34;&gt;A Real-World Comparison for People Who Actually Care About Sound&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;There’s an old joke in audio circles: “If you want no highs and no lows, buy Bose.”&lt;br&gt;&#xA;It’s been repeated for decades—mostly by people who haven’t listened to a modern pair of Bose headphones. The punchline doesn’t really land anymore, especially with the QuietComfort line. Bose has quietly built a reputation for warm, pleasant, genuinely enjoyable sound with their headphones.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
